<title>BELGIUM: EU fails to agree new farm import duty system.</title>
<headline>EU fails to agree new farm import duty system.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>European farm ministers failed to agree a Commission plan to change the way import duties on agricultural products are calculated, an EU member state official said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no change.The ministers could not agree and so the system will continue,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>The Commission had proposed ending the practice of converting some ecu-based duties into the agricultural green rate used to convert farm payments into national currencies.</p>
<p>It wanted to charge duties at the monthly customs rate used for other products.</p>
<p>&quot;Ministers could not agree and the council was told that to use the green rate for all products would discriminate against third countries and break world trade rules by increasing duties charged,&quot; the official said.</p>
</text>
